IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P5-section-5`
IMPORT `P5-art-44-45-46`

-- Tests of Articles 44, 45 and 46 (layer 1). Expected values are hand-written from the text, never from the code.
-- Dates: Chapter III Section 5 applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113 second paragraph, keel fork F-113-groups, assumed): 1 August 2026 is before, 2 August 2026 is the day, 1 September 2027 is after.
-- The Omnibus changed none of Articles 44 to 46, so there is one text: no version dispatcher and no as-enacted function. Art 111(2) matters only to Article 46(2) and (7) (a deployer, a system):
-- placed on 3 December 2027 is not saved; placed on 1 January 2027 and not significantly changed is saved on 2 December 2030, and covered if it was significantly changed.

`Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` MEANS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`

§ `Article 44(1): the language of the certificate`

-- args: date asked, the certificate is issued by a notified body in accordance with Annex VII
-- Before the group applies: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 44(1) the certificate must be drawn up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities of the Member State in which the notified body is established` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- On the day: the language duty.
#ASSERT `Art 44(1) the certificate must be drawn up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities of the Member State in which the notified body is established` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 44(1) the certificate must be drawn up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities of the Member State in which the notified body is established` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A certificate not issued in accordance with Annex VII: the paragraph does not speak (a scope limit with no 'only').
#ASSERT `Art 44(1) the certificate must be drawn up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities of the Member State in which the notified body is established` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 44(2): validity, extension and supplements`

-- args: date asked, covered by Annex I, covered by Annex III
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Annex I: five years.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 5
-- Annex III: four years.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 4
-- Both Annexes: the shorter limit binds (fork F-44-2-both).
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 4
-- Neither Annex: the sentence does not speak.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the longest period in years that a certificate may indicate` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, covered by Annex I, covered by Annex III, the first day of validity the certificate indicates, the last day of validity the certificate indicates
-- The period is computed from the two dates (fork F-44-2-period): it does not exceed the limit where the last day is at most the day before the anniversary of the first day, the limit's number of years later.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE 5 EQUALS NOTHING`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 8 2026) (Date 31 7 2031) EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
-- Five years for Annex I, from 1 January 2026 to 31 December 2030: the last day is the day before the fifth anniversary, at the limit.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
-- Six years for Annex I: 'shall not exceed'.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE 4 EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
-- Four years for Annex III: at the limit.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
-- Five years for Annex III: over the limit.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2030) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
-- Both Annexes: the shorter limit (4) binds, so five is over.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2030) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE 4 EQUALS JUST TRUE`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE 3 EQUALS NOTHING`; the caller no longer counts whole years: the certificate's first and last day of validity are two dates and the period is computed from them (fork F-44-2-period); the case is given by the dates that make the same period, the answer is unchanged
-- No limit on these facts.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 12 2028) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Five years and six months for Annex I: over the limit. A whole-years count says 5 and passes it; the dates do not (fork F-44-2-period).
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The fifth anniversary itself is a day too many (the end-day reading of fork F-44-2-period).
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- From 29 February 2028 the fifth anniversary falls in a common year and is taken as 1 March 2033, so 28 February 2033 is the last day.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE (Date 29 2 2028) (Date 28 2 2033) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the period the certificate indicates is within the limit` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE (Date 29 2 2028) (Date 1 3 2033) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, the provider has requested the extension, based on a re-assessment
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Requested and based on a re-assessment: the notified body may extend.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the Guide's In-short line gives JUST FALSE only for an if, only if, as long as, unless (or a plain variant), the rulings of 2026-11-05 add where, when, upon; 'At the request of' is none of them, so NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12 in BRIEF.md; fork F-44-2-extension).
-- No request: 'At the request of the provider' is a gate on a 'may' that is not where, when or upon (fork F-44-2-extension).
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; same reason.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Requested but not based on a re-assessment: a grant that is not made (NOTHING; fork F-44-2-extension).
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the validity of a certificate may be extended for a further period` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the supplement to a certificate remains valid` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The certificate it supplements is valid.
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the supplement to a certificate remains valid` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 'provided that the certificate which it supplements is valid' (fork F-44-2-supplement).
#ASSERT `Art 44(2) the supplement to a certificate remains valid` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Article 44(3): suspension, withdrawal, restriction, reasons and appeal`

-- args: date asked, the notified body finds that the AI system no longer meets the requirements, corrective action by the provider ensures compliance within the deadline
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A finding and no corrective action: the duty.
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 'unless compliance ... is ensured by appropriate corrective action' (fork F-44-3-unless).
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No such finding: 'Where a notified body finds' (reading (b)).
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must give reasons for its decision` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must give reasons for its decision` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- There is no decision to give reasons for.
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) the notified body must give reasons for its decision` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) an appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies must be available` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) an appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies must be available` (Date 2 8 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 44(3) an appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies must be available` (Date 1 9 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE

