§ `Article 46(1): the authorisation`

-- args: date asked, a duly justified request has been made, the reason is one of the exceptional reasons the paragraph names
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A duly justified request for an exceptional reason: the authority may authorise.
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No request: 'upon a duly justified request' (reading (b), fork F-46-1).
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` (Date 1 9 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A request for a reason the paragraph does not name: the grant is limited by 'for exceptional reasons of ...' (NOTHING; fork F-46-1).
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the market surveillance authority may authorise the placing on the market or the putting into service of a specific high-risk AI system within the territory of its Member State` (Date 1 9 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the authorisation must be for a limited period while the necessary conformity assessment procedures are being carried out` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the authorisation must be for a limited period while the necessary conformity assessment procedures are being carried out` (Date 2 8 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the completion of the conformity assessment procedures must be undertaken without undue delay` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 46(1) the completion of the conformity assessment procedures must be undertaken without undue delay` (Date 1 9 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Article 46(2): urgency without the authorisation`

-- args: date asked, route, date placed, significantly changed, the deployer is a law-enforcement or civil protection authority, a duly justified situation of urgency, the authorisation is requested during or after the use without undue delay
#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- All three: the authority may put the system into service.
#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another deployer: 'law-enforcement authorities or civil protection authorities may' (a scope limit: fork F-46-2).
#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was `#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; 'In a duly justified situation of urgency' is not where, when or upon and not an if, only if, as long as or unless, so NOTHING (Guide In-short line; ruling of 2026-11-12 in BRIEF.md; fork F-46-2).
-- No situation of urgency: 'In a duly justified situation of urgency' (a gate on a 'may' that is not where, when or upon: fork F-46-2).
#ASSERT `Art 46(2) the law-enforcement or civil protection authority may put a specific high-risk AI system into service without the authorisation` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
